  "articleBody": "Even though backsplash installation might seem straightforward, there are some common blunders that can really mess up the final look. One big mistake is skipping a dry layout – that's when you arrange your tiles on the counter or floor first to see how they'll fit. This helps you avoid ending up with tiny, awkward cut pieces at highly visible edges. Another frequent issue is installing tiles over a dirty or uneven surface; tiles need a clean, flat base to adhere correctly and look good. Using the wrong type of grout, especially for delicate materials like glass or metal tiles, can also be a problem. And finally, failing to properly finish edges or caulk change-of-plane joints (like where the backsplash meets the countertop) can leave your new backsplash looking unfinished or even prone to cracking. To get a professional result, always dry-lay your tiles, ensure your surface is clean and level, pick the right grout, and pay attention to those finishing touches. Or, even better, let a pro like HH Remodeling LLC handle it for you – we know all the tricks to make it perfect!",
